# Shell scripts and systemd units are executed on a Linux host. A checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default, and this repository is
# developed on Windows — would rewrite them to CRLF, and a CRLF shebang line
# fails at exec time with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`. That failure
# names the interpreter rather than the line ending, so it is expensive to read
# and cheap to prevent.
#
# This file did not exist before `ops/host/` did, because until then no file in
# this repository was executed by a kernel other than the one that checked it
# out. `benchmarks/run.sh` was already exposed to it and had simply not been
# run on Linux yet.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.env   text eol=lf
